{"name":"Keppel","hex":"#5fb69c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Keppel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Keppel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alice Keppel","blocks":[{"text":"Alice Frederica Keppel was an aristocrat, British society hostess and a long-time mistress of King Edward VII."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Alice_Keppel.jpg/330px-Alice_Keppel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alice_Keppel","wikidata":"Q265937"},{"title":"Arnold van Keppel, 1st Earl of Albemarle","blocks":[{"text":"Arnold Joost van Keppel, 1st Earl of Albemarle was a Dutch States Army officer who fought for William III of England and became the first Earl of Albemarle. He had a very close relationship with William and proved a capable cavalry commander. In the latter stages of the War of the Spanish Succession he sometimes assumed Dutch supreme command in absence of Claude Frédéric t'Serclaes, Count of Tilly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Arnold_Joost_van_Keppel%2C_1st_Earl_of_Albemarle_by_Sir_Godfrey_Kneller%2C_Bt.jpg/330px-Arnold_Joost_van_Keppel%2C_1st_Earl_of_Albemarle_by_Sir_Godfrey_Kneller%2C_Bt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arnold_van_Keppel%2C_1st_Earl_of_Albemarle","wikidata":"Q336005"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Duntreath_Castle%2C_Strath_Blane_-_geograph.org.uk_-_80380.jpg/500px-Duntreath_Castle%2C_Strath_Blane_-_geograph.org.uk_-_80380.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Duntreath_Castle%2C_Strath_Blane_-_geograph.org.uk_-_80380.jpg/500px-Duntreath_Castle%2C_Strath_Blane_-_geograph.org.uk_-_80380.j